{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "The session-consumption event-sequence oracle: the EXPECTED product of the ONE session consumer over a scripted ordered event sequence, read by BOTH halves of the parity gate - rust/crates/engine/degenbot-batch-executor/tests/session_consumption.rs (pure-Rust consumption) and tests/standalone_parity/test_session_consumption_gate.py (Python consumption through the PyO3 seam). Both halves feed the SAME script into the SAME Rust consumer and assert identical executor work (the per-batch outcome records, path ids, stage verdicts, blocks), identical outcome ORDERING (one record set per enqueued batch, in arrival order), identical loud-abort behavior (the first leaf failure surfaces at the consumer with its batch index and the detail), identical stall detection (the heartbeat the core stall watchdog feeds - one beat per actual stream event, so a silent source feeds none), and identical close-on-termination (the typed end verdict and the shared teardown report). Path ids are SYMBOLIC ('path_a' = the one registered 2-hop V2 path, 'path_missing' = an id the resolver does not answer); each half substitutes its own id, so the oracle holds no engine registry identity. Every raw row in a script skips pre-sim (empty hops / resolve miss / shape corruption), so no scenario dials RPC.",
